    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If you create a physics shape using one of the basic geometry classes ([`SCNBox`](scnbox.md), [`SCNSphere`](scnsphere.md), [`SCNPyramid`](scnpyramid.md), [`SCNCone`](scncone.md), [`SCNCylinder`](scncylinder.md), or [`SCNCapsule`](scncapsule.md)), SceneKit uses an idealized form of that geometry for the physics shape instead of using the geometry’s vertex data to simulate collisions.",
      "normalizedSource": "If you create a physics shape using one of the basic geometry classes ([`SCNBox`](scnbox.md), [`SCNSphere`](scnsphere.md), [`SCNPyramid`](scnpyramid.md), [`SCNCone`](scncone.md), [`SCNCylinder`](scncylinder.md), or [`SCNCapsule`](scncapsule.md)), SceneKit uses an idealized form of that geometry for the physics shape instead of using the geometry’s vertex data to simulate collisions.",
      "sourceHash": "e6e6b567b4fb371d24ba23812b57c70f2643f2976b2276b27a6a2c69423e3d2d",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "For example, if you create a physics shape from an [`SCNSphere`](scnsphere.md) object, SceneKit simulates collisions for any object that passes within the sphere’s radius.",
      "documentTitle": "init(geometry:options:)",
      "framework": "SceneKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
