      "source": "Because the idealized forms of simple geometries are computationally much simpler than the vertex data needed for displaying them, using basic geometries for physics shapes (or compound shapes created from basic geometries with the [`init(shapes:transforms:)`](scnphysicsshape/init(shapes:transforms:).md) method) often provides the best balance between simulation accuracy and performance.",
      "normalizedSource": "Because the idealized forms of simple geometries are computationally much simpler than the vertex data needed for displaying them, using basic geometries for physics shapes (or compound shapes created from basic geometries with the [`init(shapes:transforms:)`](scnphysicsshape/init(shapes:transforms:).md) method) often provides the best balance between simulation accuracy and performance.",
